  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">\"Music on the Move,\" authored by Danielle Fosler-Lussier and published by the University of Michigan Press in 2020, has garnered significant academic interest with 17 citations. It has been used as a pedagogical resource in diverse settings, evidenced by its mention in OpenCourseWare and several educational YouTube videos, attracting a total of 1,215 downloads, reflecting its active engagement within educational communities.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Despite not receiving substantial media coverage, \"Music on the Move\" stands out for its role as an essential pedagogical resource in the field of music studies, demonstrated by its high strength as a teaching anchor. The book has been integrated into various educational platforms, making it accessible for instructors and students alike. Its presence in two OpenCourseWare offerings, three YouTube lectures, and five library holdings illustrate its value as a teaching tool.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The scholarly uptake of \"Music on the Move\" is also notable, with 17 citations indicating its influence within academic discussions. These citations appear across a range of journals, indicating its interdisciplinary relevance, particularly in fields such as ethnomusicology, sociology, and globalization studies. This measure of academic engagement reflects the book's importance in contributing to ongoing scholarly dialogues.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Community discourse about the book has emerged on platforms like Wikipedia and Hypothesis, where it has sparked discussions related to the themes of migration and the role of music in cultural exchange. Such interactions suggest that the book resonates with audiences concerned with the social aspects of music, further emphasizing its relevance in contemporary discourse.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In conclusion, Danielle Fosler-Lussier's \"Music on the Move\" effectively bridges the gap between academic scholarship and practical application in education. Through its utilization in teaching and its growing citation rate, it is positioned to inspire future research and pedagogical practices across multiple disciplines.</p>",
